# XSH getppid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.getppid.001
anchor     functions/getppid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap03.html#3.253
class      required
since      1988
says       A child's getppid() returns the test process's ID, and a
           grandchild's getppid() returns the child's ID as fork() gave it
           to the test, while the child lives.
test       t/001-creator.c

assertion  XSH.getppid.002
anchor     functions/getppid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap03.html#3.253
class      required
since      1988
says       Once the child that created a grandchild has terminated and its
           status has been collected, the grandchild's getppid() returns a
           positive value other than the child's ID (the ID of a system
           process, implementation-defined).
note       Only the state after the status is collected is tested: XBD
           3.253 keeps the creator as parent for its whole lifetime (which
           XBD 3.285 ends when the ID is returned to the system), while
           _exit() reparents children at termination; both agree once the
           child is reaped (new standard issue, see the report). A reaper
           process outside the standard would also pass.
test       t/002-after-creator.c
